{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 11570,
    "dDurationMs": 5469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a water jet pack... but no, that's\nnot me flying it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17039,
    "dDurationMs": 3441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20480,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's harder than it looks, ok?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22560,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to understand how it works, we need to\nfirst talk rocket science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27150,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rocket science is meant to be one of the most\ncomplicated things in the world, but the basic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31310,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "principle is incredibly simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33570,
    "dDurationMs": 4519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just Newton's 3rd law -- all forces come\nin pairs, which are equal and opposite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38089,
    "dDurationMs": 5911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To demonstrate this, I'm using a fire extinguisher\non a skateboard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44000,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the carbon dioxide is forced out the back\nof the extinguisher, it puts a force forwards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48870,
    "dDurationMs": 13820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on me causing me to accelerate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62690,
    "dDurationMs": 6010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or that's the theory anyway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68700,
    "dDurationMs": 7400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look closely, you can spot the exact\nmoment I realize this is a fail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76100,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what was the problem here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78790,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the force applied to me by the carbon\ndioxide is equal to the rate of mass ejected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83160,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out the back of the fire extinguisher, call\nit m-dot for short, multiplied by the velocity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87960,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of that exhaust gas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89970,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this case the carbon dioxide wasn't\nejected fast enough to create a big enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94580,
    "dDurationMs": 6810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "force and overcome the small frictional forces\nto get me to accelerate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101390,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it can be done as has been demonstrated\nmany times on Youtube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105670,
    "dDurationMs": 7530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the space shuttle lifts off, exhaust\ngasses exit the nozzle at 3 to 4 km/s, ejecting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113200,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an amount of mass of 9000 kg/s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117549,
    "dDurationMs": 5741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This creates thrust equal to 30,000,000 N\nor the equivalent of about 2 million decent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123290,
    "dDurationMs": 2759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fire extinguishers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126049,
    "dDurationMs": 3611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now imagine you are an astronaut preparing\nfor launch in the space shuttle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129660,
    "dDurationMs": 5270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'd be seated not vertically but horizontally,\nperpendicular to the acceleration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134930,
    "dDurationMs": 5230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because the human body is a bit like\na water balloon where the water represents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140160,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your blood and the balloon represents your\nharder parts like your skeleton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144010,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you are accelerated up really quickly,\nthen your skeleton accelerates up at that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149570,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rate but your blood tends to stay where it\nis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152350,
    "dDurationMs": 3509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this results in the blood ending up in\nyour feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155859,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now since there's not enough oxygen going\nto your brain you would black out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160549,
    "dDurationMs": 5931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But fighter pilots face an arguably worse\nfate when they accelerate down too fast, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166480,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the blood all rushes to their head and\nthey suffer something called a red-out, where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171720,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the blood actually comes out of their eyes,\nnose, mouth, and ears."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178280,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But back to astronauts, since you are reclined,\nat worst the blood will end up in the back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182670,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your body and the back of your head, but\nyour brain will still have enough oxygen to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186700,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remain conscious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188130,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now as the spacecraft lifts off and starts\nspeeding up, the acceleration is initially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193150,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a very reasonable five to eight meters per\nsecond squared - that's less acceleration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198030,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than an object in free fall here at the surface\nof Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202120,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as the spacecraft continues to burn fuel,\nits mass decreases, while the thrust remains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208320,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentially constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209820,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now Newton's second law says that the acceleration\nof an object equals the net force applied"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214600,
    "dDurationMs": 2349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to it divided by its mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216949,
    "dDurationMs": 6211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as the mass decreases, the acceleration\nincreases -- and it increases at an increasing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223160,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224160,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So much so that at the end of the rocket burn\nthe thrust has to actually be limited in order"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229640,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep the acceleration from going over three\ng's -- that's three times the acceleration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234590,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "due to gravity or about 30 meters per second\nsquared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238730,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the term g-force has been invented to\ngive a sense of the amount of force experienced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243070,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by astronauts, in multiples of the force we\nexperience everyday."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248090,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now you are experiencing one g-force,\nprobably on your butt if you're sitting down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253230,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "-- can you feel that force?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256030,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But accelerating at three g's you would experience\nthree g-forces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260180,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the force between your back and the chair\nwould be the same as if you had two of you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264910,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stacked on top of you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267450,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, pipe down below, huh?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270900,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You guys are heavy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272960,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, man."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274000,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know that feeling when you're taking off\nin a plane and it feels like you're pressed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278120,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the seat, well really it's the seat pressing\ninto you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282640,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you imagine that feeling times 20,\nthat's what it would be like to be taking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287900,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off in the space shuttle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289660,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now an interesting side note is that we think\nof the space shuttle's acceleration as being"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293700,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mainly vertical because that's what we see\nwhen it lifts off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297620,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's actually not true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299460,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once the space shuttle exits the thicker part\nof the atmosphere, it turns horizontal and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304210,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accelerates up to its orbital velocity 28,000\nkm/h."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309250,
    "dDurationMs": 5350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So most of the acceleration of a spacecraft,\nin orbit anyway, is horizontal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314600,
    "dDurationMs": 2530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how is this like a jet pack?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317130,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well unlike the shuttle, you don't carry your\nown propellant with you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320760,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And also, there's no chemical reaction releasing\nenergy that drives the propellant downwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325700,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead the jetski pumps water out of the\nlake and up that hose at a rate up to 60 litres"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332100,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333150,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then right on these nozzles here, the\nwater changes directions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336560,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it goes from coming up to being fired out\nthe bottom, and that change in momentum as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340710,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it goes over the bend is what actually pushed\nthe jetpack up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343770,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the jetpack's pushing down on the\nwater, so by Newton's third law, the water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has to push up on the jetpack\ngenerating 1800 Newtons of thrust, that's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352480,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly equivalent to 150 decent fire extinguishers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356700,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This could accelerate me at up to 1.5 g's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360620,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you use your hands in order to steer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363170,
    "dDurationMs": 5041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lifting up to drive yourself upwards, moving\nyour hands down to accelerate forwards, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368211,
    "dDurationMs": 5789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pretend like you're turning a big wheel very\ngently in order to turn side to side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374000,
    "dDurationMs": 5670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One thing you don't want to do is try to explain\nthe physics of the jetpack while in the air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379670,
    "dDurationMs": 9610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's what I was trying to do here..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389280,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While you're learning your thrust is controlled\nby your instructor so if he sees you doing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393210,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something stupid he'll just turn off the thrust\nand drop you into the lake so you don't hurt"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397430,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398680,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's generally a good idea unless you're\non a collision course with the jetski."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404010,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I got a pretty fat lip from doing this but\nthankfully all my teeth were intact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409790,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the thrust is equal to my weight plus\nthe weight of the water in the hose, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413750,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can hover or move with constant velocity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417330,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a common misconception that you need\na little bit of unbalanced force to move with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421480,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a constant velocity -- in truth if the forces\nare balanced, you will continue moving with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426560,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whatever constant velocity you have."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428990,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other common misconception about rockets\nis that you need something to push off like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432860,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434360,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In reality, what you are pushing off is the\npropellant, so even without the air around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440240,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a water jetpack would still work because you're\npushing off the water that is coming out those"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444760,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nozzles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445760,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to go jetpacking I recommend you\ngo easy on the controls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448690,
    "dDurationMs": 5330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean the worst thing you can do is overcompensate,\nwhich I think is a typical human reaction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454020,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you're reacting to where you are and\nhow fast you're moving and you're not reacting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457920,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to acceleration which is the real thing that\nyou can control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461210,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even if you're coming down towards the\nwater quite quickly you may be slowing down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465010,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it may be ok and you don't need to adjust\nanything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467600,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You just need to trust that the jetpack will\nget you out of any trouble."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471230,
    "dDurationMs": 7630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a pretty incredibly experience, feeling\nthe power of that water rushing passed you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478860,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the closest I've gotten to flying really."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483160,
    "dDurationMs": 6550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the power of physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489710,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now many of you may not know that I have a\nsecond channel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490770,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called 2 Veritasium and I've been posting\nmore videos on there recently so if you want"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495110,
    "dDurationMs": 4809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to check them out then click on this annotation\nor the link in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499919,
    "dDurationMs": 4701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you ever want to download a Veritasium\nvideo, you can do that now via iTunes by clicking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504620,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this link and that's a service provided to\nme by Science Alert, which is one of the greatest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509230,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Facebook pages on science that exists so click\non this link if you want to check them out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514570,
    "dDurationMs": 1219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alright, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
